# Route E-commerce (Next.js)

This repo is a **Next.js App Router** storefront. The backend is the public **Route API** — we do not own the database. Do not add Laravel, Blade, Eloquent, or Olqan patterns.

- API base: `https://ecommerce.routemisr.com/api/v1`
- Docs: [Postman](https://documenter.getpostman.com/view/5709532/2s93JqTRWN) · [Route API](https://ecommerce.routemisr.com/)
- Locales: **en** + **ar** (RTL). Glossary: `docs/localization/ecommerce-arabic-glossary.md`

Before writing Next.js APIs, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (version-matched) or Context7. Do not guess App Router APIs from training data.

## 1. Architecture

- App Router only. Server Components by default. `"use client"` only for interactivity (cart qty, forms, drawers).
- Thin pages/layouts. Fetch and mutate through `lib/api/` and Server Actions — not inside JSX.
- Validate every mutation with Zod (or equivalent) in the Action / Form schema. Never trust client payloads.
- Typed API client only. Never `fetch` Route URLs ad hoc from components.
- Cart mutations use **`/api/v2/cart`** (populated, consistent). Other resources stay on `/api/v1`.
- Auth header for Route is `token` (raw JWT), not `Authorization: Bearer`.
- Store the JWT in an **httpOnly, Secure, SameSite** cookie. Server Actions / Route Handlers attach `token`. Do not put the JWT in `localStorage` or client JS.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — token in the browser, fetch in a component
localStorage.setItem('token', jwt);
await fetch('https://ecommerce.routemisr.com/api/v1/cart', { headers: { token: jwt } });

// ✅ GOOD — cookie + server-side client
await api.cart.add(productId); // Server Action reads cookie, sends token header
```

## 2. Validation & state

- Required fields, types, and edge cases in Zod schemas colocated with the Action.
- Reject invalid transitions (checkout with empty cart, qty < 1, unauthenticated cart writes).
- Map Route API errors (`message`, `errors`, `statusMsg`) to user-facing copy via i18n keys — never dump raw API JSON in the UI.

## 3. Security (Critical)

- No secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`. Base URL may be public; tokens and Stripe session secrets must not.
- Escape all user/API text in React (`{value}`). Flag every `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- No open redirects after login. Allowlist internal paths only.
- Do not log JWTs, passwords, or reset codes.
- Server-side auth checks on every protected Action (cart, wishlist, addresses, orders). Client `useAuth()` is UX only.

## 4. Performance

- Parallelize independent server fetches (`Promise.all`). No request waterfalls.
- Cache public catalog (products, categories, brands) with Next.js `fetch` cache / `revalidate`. Never cache authenticated cart/orders as public.
- Paginate product lists. Use Route `limit` + `page`. Do not load the full catalog into the client.
- Images: `next/image` with remote patterns for Route CDN hosts.
- Keep client bundles small: do not import server-only API modules into Client Components.

## 5. UI (React / Tailwind)

- Views render prepared data only. No Route `fetch` inside Client Components.
- Reuse components for repeated product-card / form patterns. YAGNI: extract only at 2+ callers.
- Named routes via `next/link` + next-intl pathnames — never hardcoded `/en/products/123` strings in multiple files.
- Always `{{ }}`-style escaped output (JSX default). Forms that mutate need the same CSRF/cookie posture as Actions.

## 6. Localization (en + ar)

Glossary always wins: `docs/localization/ecommerce-arabic-glossary.md`.

- Every new `messages/en/*.json` key MUST have the same key in `messages/ar/`.
- Buttons use **noun form**: Save → حفظ, Edit → تعديل, Delete → حذف, Add → إضافة.
- Success messages begin with **تم**. Do not translate brand names (Stripe, Google).
- Use `next-intl` (`useTranslations` / `getTranslations`), never hardcoded UI copy.

## 7. RTL

- Root `dir` from locale (`ar` → `rtl`). Never hardcode `dir="ltr"` on page shells.
- CSS **logical properties** only: `margin-inline-start`, `text-align: start`, `inset-inline-start`.
- Directional icons must mirror in RTL; trash/edit/close must not.
- Format dates/numbers/currency with locale-aware formatters. EGP symbol follows Arabic conventions.

## 8. Review output

For every issue: problem, why it matters, concrete fix, severity (**Critical / High / Medium / Low**).

## 9. MCP (use these; skip the rest)

| When | MCP |
|------|-----|
| Next.js API / caching / App Router | **Context7** (`/vercel/next.js`) or `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` |
| Running app errors, routes, logs | **next-devtools-mcp** (add when scaffolding; needs `next dev`) |
| UI components | **shadcn** (app UI) · **Magic UI** (marketing motion only) |
| Click / a11y / e2e verification | **Playwright** |
| Perf traces, hydration | **chrome-devtools** |
| Production errors (after Sentry is wired) | **Sentry** |

Do **not** use Customer.io, Greptile, ReUI, or Stitch unless the user asks. Firecrawl is optional for refreshing Route/Postman docs.

## 10. Guard skills

Do **not** run every skill on every change. Match the stage.

**A) Before coding (optional)**

1. `grill-with-docs` — "grill this", "stress-test this plan"
2. `impeccable` → `shape` — new UI flow before implementation

**B) After finishing code (ship gate)** — skip layers that did not change

1. **`nextjs-architecture-guard`** — pages, layouts, Actions, `lib/api` ("guard architecture", "thin page")
2. **`clean-code-guard`** — always on changed TS/TSX/JS ("guard this")
3. **`test-guard`** — if tests changed ("guard tests")
4. **`nextjs-security`** — auth, cookies, cart, checkout, uploads ("security audit")
5. **UI** — pick one: `impeccable` / `web-design-guidelines` / `critique` / `clarify`
6. **`vercel-react-best-practices`** — waterfalls, bundles, "make it faster"
7. **`code-review-expert`** — last pass ("final review")

Default: `guard architecture` → `guard this` → (`guard tests`) → (`security audit` if sensitive) → (`ui review` if UI) → `final review`

**C) Stuck:** `systematic-debugging` before more edits.

**D) Meta:** `find-skills` · `caveman` (only if asked)

